WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.045
Jimmy's family was on their way to a beach vacation.

2
00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:12.883
As they drove along, his parents and twin brother Jason were talking excitedly.

3
00:00:12.884 --> 00:00:18.838
"I'm going to walk on the beach every morning," Mom said.

4
00:00:18.839 --> 00:00:23.027
"I'm going fishing," Dad said.

5
00:00:23.028 --> 00:00:27.716
"Can we go to the amusement park?" Jason asked.

6
00:00:27.717 --> 00:00:33.008
"There's a new roller coaster—Motion Monster."

7
00:00:33.009 --> 00:00:36.689
Jimmy stayed quiet.

8
00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:43.583
"What's wrong, Jimmy?" Mom asked.

9
00:00:43.584 --> 00:00:48.077
He shrugged. "Nothing."

10
00:00:48.078 --> 00:00:52.720
"I know what's wrong!" Jason grinned.

11
00:00:52.721 --> 00:00:56.707
"This is a long car ride.

12
00:00:56.708 --> 00:01:01.541
He's worried he's going to throw up!"

13
00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:05.168
"I brought some stuff, in case you do feel carsick."

14
00:01:05.169 --> 00:01:08.088
Mom held up a bag.

15
00:01:08.089 --> 00:01:14.529
"I've got peppermint gum, ginger candy, wristbands, and even some medicine.

16
00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:17.831
One of these treatments might help."

17
00:01:17.832 --> 00:01:25.960
Jimmy sighed. "Why do I get carsick anyway?"

18
00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:30.508
"It's called motion sickness," Mom said.

19
00:01:30.509 --> 00:01:35.847
"It comes from your ears and your eyes having a disagreement."

20
00:01:35.848 --> 00:01:42.875
"Kind of like . . ." Jimmy looked at Jason. "Twins disagreeing?"

21
00:01:42.876 --> 00:01:46.539
"Not exactly," Mom said.

22
00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:53.217
"Motion sickness occurs when one sense detects motion, but another one does not.

23
00:01:53.218 --> 00:01:59.101
For example, if you're reading in the car, your eyes think you're staying still.

24
00:01:59.102 --> 00:02:04.964
Meanwhile your ears detect motion, and the two senses clash."

25
00:02:04.965 --> 00:02:08.744
"So your brain gets different messages," Dad added.

26
00:02:08.745 --> 00:02:16.063
"And you start to sweat or feel sick to your stomach."

27
00:02:16.064 --> 00:02:20.590
"I never get carsick," Jason bragged.

28
00:02:20.591 --> 00:02:27.301
"Doctors aren't sure why some people get motion sickness and others do not," Mom said.

29
00:02:27.302 --> 00:02:32.055
"But it's very common, especially among kids."

30
00:02:32.056 --> 00:02:38.386
"Grandma gets motion sickness on airplanes," Dad said.

31
00:02:38.387 --> 00:02:42.127
"My friend Shin gets seasick on boats.

32
00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:48.344
He eats ginger before he goes sailing—that's what Chinese fishermen have done for centuries.

33
00:02:48.345 --> 00:02:49.844
It calms your stomach.

34
00:02:49.845 --> 00:02:55.505
Another trick is to stare at the horizon when you're seasick."

35
00:02:55.506 --> 00:03:01.865
"Uh-oh . . ." Jimmy could see that their car was approaching a curvy road.

36
00:03:01.866 --> 00:03:08.850
"Here." Mom handed him the gum.

37
00:03:08.851 --> 00:03:12.839
"The doctor said peppermint is good for stomachaches.

38
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.937
Roll down your window for fresh air.

39
00:03:15.938 --> 00:03:19.547
Don't read or look at a screen."

40
00:03:19.548 --> 00:03:22.504
Jimmy followed his mom's advice.

41
00:03:22.505 --> 00:03:28.115
As the car drove along the road, he chewed gum and closed his eyes.

42
00:03:28.116 --> 00:03:33.075
"How's it going?" Mom asked.

43
00:03:33.076 --> 00:03:39.779
He took a deep breath. "Good! I feel fine!"

44
00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:45.835
The week at the beach flew by.

45
00:03:45.836 --> 00:03:51.168
One cloudy day the family went to the amusement park.

46
00:03:51.169 --> 00:03:56.956
"Whoa, check it out!" Jason pointed to Motion Monster.

47
00:03:56.957 --> 00:04:07.795
It was an enormous roller coaster with steep hills and huge loops. "Let's go!"

48
00:04:07.796 --> 00:04:13.839
The twins raced over to the ride and hopped into the first car.

49
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:21.152
Minutes later they began going up the first slope.

50
00:04:21.153 --> 00:04:26.402
"Ahh!" Jason screamed as they flew downward.

51
00:04:26.403 --> 00:04:36.634
Jimmy threw his arms up. "Whee! This is awesome!"

52
00:04:36.635 --> 00:04:42.290
But when he looked over at his twin, he saw Jason clutching his stomach.

53
00:04:42.291 --> 00:04:51.968
"What's wrong?" Jimmy asked. But he already knew the answer.

54
00:04:51.969 --> 00:05:01.124
Jason had motion sickness!

